&lt;p&gt;The Technical Content team is looking for an experienced Content Optimization Specialist who will help grow the visibility of Datadog across traditional search and AI-assisted search platforms. As part of the Community organization, you will optimize written and video technical content for search engines, answer engines, generative engines, and AI/LLM experiences while identifying new opportunities as audience needs and search behavior continue to evolve. You should understand how content is surfaced, cited, and summarized across traditional search, AI-assisted search, and agentic platforms. The ideal candidate has hands-on experience optimizing content that targets search demand from a highly technical audience and wants to apply their skills to the evolving AEO/GEO landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace, in the office three days per week, to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical concepts into clear, well-structured content that aligns with audience-specific search intent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage on-page content optimization, including metadata, structure, and internal linking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze how Datadog content is surfaced, cited, and summarized across AI-assisted search and agentic platforms, and use those findings to guide content optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders across our Community, Marketing, and Product Management teams to ensure content aligns with SEO/AEO/GEO best practices and supports key growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct keyword research and content gap analysis that inform content production and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create content briefs and outlines that turn research findings into clear requirements for content development and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and report on the results of content optimization efforts, highlighting gains, losses, and opportunities across search rankings, earned citations, AI visibility, traffic, and user engagement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience creating a high volume of technically accurate content for an engineering and developer audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a portfolio of content you’ve developed in previous roles and can show how your work contributed to measurable business results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3-5 years of hands-on SEO experience, with a focus on on-page content optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 1-2 years of experience optimizing content for AI-assisted search and agentic platforms (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Codex, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proficient with several SEO/AEO tools, such as Profound, Conductor, Semrush, Ahrefs, and Google Search Console.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 2-5 years of experience working as a technical content writer, journalist, or content strategist at an AI or SaaS company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You stay up to date on SEO, AEO, GEO, and AI trends and know how to translate industry changes into opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
