&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director, Enterprise Customer Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, Enterprise Customer Success, you will own the strategy, operations, and outcomes for our largest and most strategic customer relationships while leading a team of 25+ Customer Success Managers through multiple first-line managers. You&#39;ll be accountable for the retention and expansion of a significant portion of Datadog&#39;s enterprise book in EMEA, while building and scaling the org, systems, and talent needed to do that sustainably. This is a chance to shape how a market-leading company runs enterprise customer success at scale, with direct visibility into your impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategic and operational health of your book of business, accountable for product adoption, retention, and customer experience outcomes across our largest accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of first-line managers, building their management capability so they in turn build strong teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and run the team&#39;s operating rhythm: forecast reviews, QBR/EBR cadence, and the metrics (e.g. consumption, NRR, health scores) that tell you where to intervene&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the executive escalation point when needed for strategic accounts, stepping into complex or high-stakes customer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale the department: design org structure, drive hiring to meet growth targets, and build career pathing for managers and ICs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to shape account growth strategy, co-design onboarding and everboarding curriculum, and align hiring plans with the broader EMEA enterprise business&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with stakeholder departments to actualize on account growth strategies, team operations, co-design an everboarding training curriculum, and meet hiring goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically partner with Enterprise Sales leadership to align on growth strategy across existing and new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion practical AI adoption across the team by identifying where AI tools genuinely improve efficiency or customer outcomes, and coaching managers and CSMs to use them well without eroding judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone with 8+ years leading Customer Success or Account Management teams in SaaS, including 3+ years managing managers (leading a team of comparable or greater scale)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning retention/expansion outcomes and using data like NRR/GRR, health scoring, and churn and renewal forecasting, to run and coach a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and scaling teams across established and emerging geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-fluent: comfortable using AI tools in your own workflow and identifying where they create real opportunity for a customer success organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with observability and/or security software in B2B tech preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your experience, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
