&lt;p&gt;As Senior Group Manager of Experience Design on Datadog&#39;s Web Experience team, you will lead and grow the Experience Design group while remaining hands-on with the web experiences that matter most to our customers and business. You will manage two designers today and help shape how the team scales over time. You will set a high bar for craft and execution across research, journey mapping, interaction design, prototyping, implementation, and post-launch quality. You will also evolve AI-assisted and code-connected design workflows, partnering closely with Product Marketing, Growth, Web Engineering, and Web Content Engineering to move from ideas to shipped experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow the Experience Design group, managing two designers today and helping shape the team as its scope evolves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach, develop, and set clear expectations for designers while maintaining a high bar for design craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design priority web experiences from journey mapping and research through interaction design, prototyping, and shipped pages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype with AI and working code, use Figma MCP and Code Connect to keep design and implementation aligned, and work directly in the CMS when appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the team’s design process across discovery, critique, specification, handoff, and post-launch quality assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing, Growth, Web Engineering, and Web Content Engineering to shape priorities and deliver web experiences that support business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced across UX/UI, journey mapping, and web design, with a portfolio of shipped, high-traffic marketing or product marketing experiences and particular depth in web and product experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A people leader who remains actively involved in design work and is comfortable moving between team leadership and hands-on execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using code as part of the design process, including prototyping, reading implementation details, working with Figma MCP and Code Connect, and building within a modern CMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced using AI to prototype, explore design directions, and reduce repetitive work, with a thoughtful perspective on where AI adds value to the design process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced hiring, coaching, and developing designers, including giving actionable feedback and supporting specialists with deep expertise in their disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We understand not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That&#39;s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your skills, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow an Experience Design function while continuing to work directly on complex, high-impact design challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape how the team approaches design craft, critique, research, prototyping, implementation, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand your experience with AI-assisted prototyping, code-connected design workflows, and CMS-based delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with marketing, growth, engineering, and content partners on priorities across Datadog’s web experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define how the Experience Design team scales as its scope and responsibilities evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
